summary:
- topic: Meeting Decorum
  text: The meeting began with the Chair addressing previous decorum issues and setting
    expectations for respectful dialogue and public participation.
- topic: Budget Update & Health Insurance
  text: The Assistant Superintendent provided a budget update, noting a lower-than-expected
    health insurance increase, which freed up $655,000 for the local budget.
- topic: Financial Stability & Contingency
  text: Discussion focused on building financial stability through fund balance, reserves,
    and contingency, with the administration recommending increasing contingency in
    the FY27 budget.
- topic: Reinstatement of Positions
  text: Proposed budget changes included reinstating two elementary classroom teachers
    (as one-year positions), two special education ed techs, one SPTA related arts
    teacher at the middle school, and an elementary behavior support (BCBA) role.
- topic: Reconfiguration Concerns
  text: Board members and the public raised significant concerns about the costs,
    implementation plan, and timeline for elementary school reconfiguration, particularly
    its impact on special education staffing, safety, and teacher workload.
- topic: Public Comment Limits
  text: A motion was passed to limit public comment sessions to 75 minutes each, with
    individual speakers limited to three minutes and no yielding of time.
- topic: FY27 Budget Adoption
  text: The board voted 4-2 to adopt the FY27 superintendent's budget as their proposal
    to the city council, acknowledging that it is not the final form and further discussions
    are anticipated.
- topic: Staffing and Safety
  text: Numerous public speakers, including teachers and parents, voiced strong concerns
    about staffing levels in special education classrooms, safety issues, and the
    impact of cuts on student-facing positions and related arts programs.
